\\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -7 \\\\ 3 \\end{pmatrix} + u \\begin{pmatrix} -1 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}.\\]If $\\theta$ is the acute angle formed by the two lines, then find $\\cos \\theta.$","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"b1395f7f47048dbb1a911908d332199f2003458e51553c3a567f3f2b2a2246b7"},"seconds":15.334657669067383,"seed":1146497978050466757,"stop":"eos","text":"To find the cosine of the acute angle \\(\\theta\\) formed by the two lines, we need to use the direction vectors of the lines. The direction vector of the first line is \\(\\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}\\) and the direction vector of the second line is \\(\\begin{pmatrix} -1 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}\\).\n\nThe formula for the cosine of the angle \\(\\theta\\) between two vectors \\(\\mathbf{a}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{b}\\) is given by:\n\\[\n\\cos \\theta = \\frac{\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}}{\\|\\mathbf{a}\\| \\|\\mathbf{b}\\|}\n\\]\nwhere \\(\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}\\) is the dot product of \\(\\mathbf{a}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{b}\\), and \\(\\|\\mathbf{a}\\|\\) and \\(\\|\\mathbf{b}\\|\\) are the magnitudes of \\(\\mathbf{a}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{b}\\), respectively.\n\nFirst, we calculate the dot product \\(\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}\\):\n\\[\n\\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{pmatrix} -1 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix} = 2 \\cdot (-1) + 1 \\cdot 1 = -2 + 1 = -1\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate the magnitudes of the vectors \\(\\mathbf{a}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{b}\\):\n\\[\n\\|\\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}\\| = \\sqrt{2^2 + 1^2} = \\sqrt{4 + 1} = \\sqrt{5}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\|\\begin{pmatrix} -1 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}\\| = \\sqrt{(-1)^2 + 1^2} = \\sqrt{1 + 1} = \\sqrt{2}\n\\]\n\nNow, we substitute these values into the formula for the cosine of the angle:\n\\[\n\\cos \\theta = \\frac{-1}{\\sqrt{5} \\cdot \\sqrt{2}} = \\frac{-1}{\\sqrt{10}} = -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} = -\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{10}\n\\]\n\nSince we are asked for the cosine of the acute angle, we take the absolute value of the result:\n\\[\n\\cos \\theta = \\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{10}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{10}}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{10}}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"precalculus:458"}
